{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Option A implemented (operator-approved 2026-08-28) — change pushed for review\n\nExecuted the ticket's recommended disposition: the decimal-string wire form for\nout-of-JS-safe-range integers now applies to CLI `--output json` (and `--output llm`),\nnot just MCP.\n\n### Reuse, not rewrite\n`js_safe_result` (`src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py`) and `install_js_safe_guard` are UNTOUCHED —\nchange 2336 depends on `js_safe_result` directly. The change is purely additive: a thin\n`js_safe_dumps(value, **kwargs)` wrapper beside it (`json.dumps(js_safe_result(value), **kwargs)`)\nplus imports at the CLI emitters. Nothing was moved, renamed, or refactored.\n\n### Surfaces changed — measured unsafe ints (`|n| > 2**53-1`) before → after\n| command | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rebar show --output json` | 4 | 0 |\n| `rebar list --output json` | 2 | 0 |\n| `rebar ready --output json` | 3 | 0 |\n| `rebar sign --output json` | 1 | 0 |\n| `rebar verify-signature --output json` | 1 | 0 |\n| `rebar audit show --output json` | 4 | 0 |\n\n`search`, `session-logs`, `deps`, `summary`, `review-plan --status` and the `--output llm`\nprojections ride the same emitters and are covered.\n\n### Library finding (asked for explicitly)\nThe `import rebar` facade has **one** JSON serialization boundary, not zero: `rebar.export_tickets()`\n/ `iter_export_states()` → `rebar._io.export_ndjson` writes NDJSON with `json.dumps`\n(`src/rebar/_io/export_ndjson.py:168`). Every OTHER library read returns Python `int`s\n(arbitrary-precision, no JSON boundary) and is genuinely N/A, as this ticket's Notes said.\nExport was deliberately left unchanged here — it is a separately versioned interop projection\n(`EXPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION`) with a round-trip contract against `rebar import`, so retyping it needs\na coordinated import-side change. Measured post-fix it still reports 4 unsafe ints. Filed as\n`guilty-pusslike-wyvern` (`a8db-dc3c-983a-40b0`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\n### Schema prose\nNo schema change was needed. `ticket_state` / `common` / `sign_result` /\n`verify_signature_result` / `plan_review_status` already type these fields\n`[\"integer\",\"string\",…]` and already describe the string WIRE FORM with **no surface\nqualifier**. That prose was true only of MCP until now; it is now literally true. The\nrelease-notes claim that \"CLI `--output json` … UNCHANGED\" was the inaccurate half and is\nmarked superseded.\n\n### Evidence\nRED first: 8 tests failing for the right reason, then green. Mutation-checked twice\n(`--color=no` + explicit returncode):\n- guard disabled (`json.dumps(value)`) → 8/8 fail;\n- `str(int(float(value)))` lossy-string mutant → the exact-round-trip oracle\n  `test_show_timestamp_round_trips_exactly` FAILS, which is the point: a type-only assertion\n  survives that mutant.\n\nGates: `make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0 (683 files), `test_module_size_contract` 4 passed,\n`check_complexity_baseline --check` `new=0 increased=0`, `scripts/probe_rebar.py` 142/0,\nfull `tests/interfaces` tier 2215 passed / 10 skipped.\n\nNote on claim: this ticket was already `in_progress` (left claimed by the parked RCA session);\n`rebar claim` refuses with \"status is in_progress, not open\", so the claim step was already\nsatisfied. No `--force` was used anywhere.\n\nLeaving `in_progress` until the Gerrit change is `Verified +1` and merged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787955096864903197,"uuid":"d47933e6-c6c4-4c5b-8a25-ccc7153b41b1"}